  "behavior": {
    "semantics": "Local RAW listening is stereo I/Q audio at the selected device clock: I left, Q right, nominal 0.3 headroom times configured audio gain and native volume. Receiver IQ correction and RF decimation remain active; the mono voice EQ/AGC/pitch chain is bypassed. Full-band IQ export remains at the original RF clock.",
    "conversion": "The verified shared complex FIR decimator bounds high-rate input. Independent shared fractional-delay FIR filters preserve channel identity, filter before rate conversion and retain history across input chunks. Equal clocks preserve sanitized scaled I/Q exactly without adding filter delay.",
    "clock": "Represent the actual f64 input clock as an exact dyadic ratio. Bounded integer phase gives ceil(N * output Fs / input Fs) frames without accumulated clock drift. Defer frames beyond root input duration when coarse conversion produces an entire stride. Preceding floor(N/D) RF decimation contributes a causal zero startup interval; a separate root-duration budget preserves capture length including tiny blocks and incomplete strides.",
    "publication": "RAW native playback and RadioAudio carry two interleaved channels at the device rate; snapshot sample counts remain frames. Voice/WFM WAV publication retains its existing mono convention. GUI output reopens with two input channels for local RAW, independently of the WFM stereo option.",
    "recording": "RAW WAV headers and metadata declare two channels. Native WAV ingress rejects channel/packet geometry changes, stores scalar audio_samples and per-channel audio_frames separately, and computes duration from frames/rate. Main recorder metadata retains channels/frame count. The RF sample clock remains separate from audio clock."
  },
